Crystallized Ginger, with its addictive flavor profile, can go anywhere ginger goes. If sugar content is a concern, rinse the sugar off and chop as you would chop a piece of ginger root. Use it as the savory base for a curry and sauté it in with the onions at the start of your cook time. Add it to Spiced Anise and Ginger Beef. Chop and mix with hot peppers, and fresh mint for a spicy relish, or balance the sweetness of Crystallized Ginger with vinegar for a robust chutney. Ginger pairs well with salmon, so try it with Salmon Charmoula or Salmon with Spinach in a Ginger and Soy Asian Broth. It also can be finely chopped and used for baking and sweet treats like warm Cinnamon Scones. Mix it into carrot cake batter, sprinkle it as a garnish for cupcakes, and mix it in ice cream for a spicy-cold kick.
