chip, tortilla, sauce, salt, and nuts and seeds manufacturers;
sausage and meat processors;
BBQ, Latin American, Mediterranean, Mexican, and seafood restaurants;
brewpubs;
seasoning companies; and
olive oil shops
Please visit our paprika page to browse the varieties of paprika available.

Flavor Profile
Smoked Sweet Paprika has earthy, mild chile flavor, complexity, and smoky depth.

How to Use
Smoked Sweet Paprika adds an earthy chile base and smoky depth to a wide variety of dishes. Use it in sauces, sausages, and rubs, or wherever you want a mild, rich chile base. Its also has a terrific, bold red color that makes attractive rubs and is distinctively eye-catching when sprinkled over finished foods as a garnish. In the United States, many competition barbecuers use Smoked Sweet Paprika as a secret ingredient in their pork rubs.
Smoked Paprika is added to sausage, DIY grill rubs and seasoning blends for meats and fish, meatloaf, vegetables, rice, sauces, soups, stews, salad dressings, garnishes, and eggs.
Smoked Paprika pairs well with allspice, caraway, cardamom, garlic, ginger, oregano, parsley, pepper, rosemary, saffron, thyme, and turmeric.

