Spicy Pumpkin Pie Spice is a salt-free, MSG-free spin on a modern classic. It is also referred to as hot pumpkin pie spice, spicy pumpkin pie seasoning, zesty pumpkin spice, warm pumpkin pie spice, hot pumpkin spice, or spicy pumpkin spice.
The first commercial pumpkin spice blend emerged on the scene in the 1930s, but was generally regarded as a purely seasonal product with one use, and that was for pumpkin pies. 2003 ushered in a new era for pumpkin spice, first appearing in lattes and then, in just about everything else. While its demand is still primarily seasonal, the flavors are classic and with our introduction of spicy elements, it crosses the line to savory use with ease.
